REGENT OF MELAWI

WEST KALIMANTAN PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF MELAWI REGENCY

NUMBER 15 OF 2017

CONCERNING

THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION OF WOMEN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF MELAWI,

a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security from all forms of violence;

b. that all forms of acts of violence against women constitute violations of human rights, therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected, and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;

c. that violence against women continues to increase, therefore protection efforts are needed; d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional

Regulation concerning

the Implementation of Protection of Women from

Acts of Violence;

In View of 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

